+# Todo Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Implement ticket #1: optional calendar due dates and consistent UTC overdue status, with API and list filtering.
+
+**Architecture:** The in-memory store owns date validation and dynamically derived overdue status. HTTP passes the validated filter to the store. The existing HTML page requests and renders the chosen API list when its checkbox changes.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, built-in HTTP, node:test, browser DOM; zero dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-todo-due-date-design.md` (approved by user).
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Optional pure calendar date `YYYY-MM-DD`; missing/null on POST means no date; omitted on PATCH preserves it, null removes it.
+- Every todo response includes `dueDate` (date or null) and `overdue` (Boolean).
+- Overdue means open, dated, strictly before today UTC; compute at response time in the store.
+- Invalid date values and invalid overdue filter values produce ValidationError / HTTP 400.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` filters; absent or `overdue=false` returns all in original order.
+- Exact checkbox copy: `nur überfällige`; initially unchecked; data-testid `overdue-filter`.
+- Display `Fällig: YYYY-MM-DD` and, only when overdue, `Überfällig`; retain existing title/done display.
+- No dependencies, editing forms, sorting, additional filters, reminders, or persistence.
+- Write failing tests in `test/` before implementation. Agent runs Playwright E2E, stores evidence outside repository, and shuts down app.
+- Draft PR only, base `main`, branch `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`; never merge or close ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Gregorian century boundaries: reject 1900-02-29, accept 2000-02-29; reject rollover dates rather than silently normalizing (Task 1).
+- Long-lived store crossing UTC midnight: overdue status must change without writes; host timezone must not affect it (Task 1).
+- Invalid multi-field PATCH: title, done and dueDate must all remain unchanged on error (Task 1).
+- Query values such as empty, `1`, or `TRUE`: return 400, never silently filter (Task 2).
+- Rapid checkbox changes with out-of-order HTTP completion: final displayed list must follow current checkbox state (Task 3).
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store date validation, dynamic responses and filtering
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/store.mjs`; create `test/store.test.mjs`; update the exact response expectation in `test/app.test.mjs`.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces `createStore({ now = () => new Date() } = {})`, with existing methods unchanged except optional `list({ overdue = false } = {})`.
+- Todo responses: `{ id, title, done, dueDate, overdue }`; raw stored records exclude overdue.
+- `add({ title, dueDate = null })`; `update(id, patch)` validates all fields before mutating.
+- Derived response objects must not expose mutable stored records; client `overdue` values are ignored.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Write store tests** using `createStore({ now: () => new Date(instant) })` and table-driven invalid values. Pin these assertions:
+
+```js
+assert.deepEqual(store.add({ title: 'A' }),
+  { id: 1, title: 'A', done: false, dueDate: null, overdue: false });
+// instant initially 2026-10-23T23:59:59.999Z
+assert.equal(store.add({ title: 'today', dueDate: '2026-10-23' }).overdue, false);
+instant = '2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z';
+assert.equal(store.get(2).overdue, true);
+assert.equal(store.update(2, { done: true }).overdue, false);
+assert.equal(store.update(2, { dueDate: null }).dueDate, null);
